  "source_semantics_evidence": [
    "Closed as not planned",
    "Closed as not planned",
    "Python 3.14.3 introduced a behavior change of how `run_in_executor` interacts with `call_soon_threadsafe`. Previously, callbacks scheduled via `call_soon_threadsafe` from within an executor job were guaranteed to run before `await run_in_executor()` returned.",
    "> Previously, callbacks scheduled via call_soon_threadsafe from within an executor job were guaranteed to run before await run_in_executor() returned.",
    "Hmm, AFAIK this was never guaranteed, it just happened to work like that on previous versions. If you change the `call_soon` to `call_later` with small delay such as `0.001` in `intermediate_callback` then you would see this behaviour on older versions as well.",
    "closed this as 【75†not planned】【76†on Mar 21, 2026】"
  ],
